From 074a021a4d1f92841575d3c18c84355af90e4cb1 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Lumnus <lumnus.org@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 4 Nov 2026 09:08:03 +0000
Subject: [PATCH 52/53] B70-CJK: serving-side Han mask with a per-request auto
 gate (B70_CJK_MASK=1, default off)

Boot builds one device bool mask [vocab] from the tokenizer: tokens whose
byte-level text holds Han (U+3400-4DBF, U+4E00-9FFF, U+F900-FAFF) plus
incomplete-UTF-8 byte tokens led by 0xE3-0xE9/0xEF whose range reaches Han
and not kana (lone 0xE3 / 0xEF kept so kana stays emittable). QFN: 55,659 of
248,320 ids (55,328 Han + 331 partial).

The model runner applies it in place on the target logits after
compute_logits, beside the grammar bitmask: one Triton launch over flagged
rows, skipped on the host when no row is flagged. Covers the plain sampler,
every spec-decode verification row (stock and B70_SAMPLER_FAST), and declines
the astra greedy shortcut for flagged batches.

Per request: on unless the system/developer/user turns hold Han; explicit
vllm_xargs.cjk_mask (or top-level cjk_mask) wins. Chat resolves in the
protocol; other endpoints fall back to a prompt-token scan in the input
processor. Env unset: stock behaviour.
